Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:00.709 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  for russia the war in ukraine has been a  disaster  in just over two months around 15 000  soldiers have been killed  including an estimated 10 generals  at least 1 800 armored vehicles have  been destroyed  [Music]  and the attempt to take over the capital  kiev was a chaotic failure resulting in  a humiliating retreat  so what's wrong with the russian army  there's a debate swirling among western  military officers experts officials as  to why the russian army has done so  badly in ukraine and part of the answer  is they were set up to fail they were  told to invade ukraine and they were  told that the country would collapse  quickly so they didn't plan properly and  they initially attempted a botched  effort at regime change with a very  lightly armed force but then what we saw  when the russian army did invade in  large numbers was a campaign that was  not only planned very badly but also  executed very badly we saw tactical  errors we saw low morale we saw a  russian air force that was nearly absent  from the campaign in modern armies the  principle of jointness is really valued  and that means army air force navy and  other branches like cyber forces  electronic warfare and and marines all  working hand in glove  russia's army has shown that it isn't  any good at that russian troops out  there in the field facing ukrainians are  not getting the kind of air support that  a american ground force or a british  ground force would enjoy from the air  one factor that we have to bear in mind  is that russia's army does not have a  layer of what in western armies we call  non-commissioned officers or ncos this  is a layer of of men or women who are  senior enlisted personnel they're not  officers uh but they are sort of  enlisted men who have been in the force  for many years and supervise train and  discipline the uh privates the the  people under them this is a vital layer  of leadership for instilling discipline  in any western army the russian army  doesn't have it and i think we are  seeing the consequences of that in  ukraine today  russia's army has always had a fairly  brutal way of warfare we saw this in  afghanistan in the 1980s in chechnya in  the 1990s and early 2000s and of course  in their intervention in support of  bashar al-assad syria's dictator from  2015 and we have now seen it again in  evidence of war crimes in places like  bucha a suburb of kiev and other parts  of ukraine there are probably two  reasons for brutality one of them is  that it can be instrumental it can be a  way of terrorizing the civilian  population to make it easier to control  them to subdue any kind of resistance or  revolt  the other fact of course is that this is  a undisciplined army uh there are  conscripts who are young 18 year olds  perhaps from far away parts of russia  who were never told they were going to  ukraine let alone to fight and have  found themselves uh in these scenarios  in these situations uh very poorly led  uh they are being fed rations that may  be expired they are cold they may be  hungry they may be demoralized and they  may have suffered grave casualties  in those conditions under those  circumstances it's no surprise that an  army may resort to abuses that it may  turn itself and turn its weapons onto  the civilian population a poorly led  army an undisciplined army is not just a  poor fighting force it's also a hazard  to the civilians amongst whom it fights  the battle for the donbass region that  is now unfolding is absolutely critical  for both sides if russia fails to make  significant gains in donbass over the  next few weeks  it will constitute a strategic failure  for the russian army and indeed the  combat power of the russian army will be  spent it will have suffered too many  casualties too much attrition to mount  another attack on kiev or other cities  and i think vladimir putin will then be  facing a difficult and unpalatable and  indeed a dangerous choice between  backing down and giving up on ukraine or  conducting a national mobilization of  manpower and equipment and resources and  escalating in the country so that is  what makes this next few weeks so vital  for ukraine for russia and for the west  thank you for watching for all our  coverage on the war in ukraine please  click on the link and don't forget to  subscribe  you

